# UI states and forms

## Five required states

Every page, section and list handles: loading, empty, error, no-permission, and guest (when the SRS defines a
guest error path). Use the shared components (`LoadingState`/skeletons, `EmptyState`, `ErrorState`,
`NoPermissionState`, `GuestPromptState` — exact names in `docs/10-design-system.md`). No one-off inline versions.
Today only `EmptyState` and `PanelLoadingOverlay` exist. If a needed state component is missing, create it once in
`components/ui/` (with a `/dev/ui-kit` demo) instead of writing an inline version.
Empty states use the SRS text when the SRS gives one (e.g. "گفتگوی شخصی برای نمایش وجود ندارد").
Search/filter with no result uses the SRS "no result" text, distinct from the empty state.

## Forms

- One Zod schema per form, shared by client and server. Client validation is UX; the server is authoritative.
  Applies to new forms; existing manual forms (e.g. `auth-forms.tsx`) migrate when substantially changed.
- Field rules (required, min/max length, formats, file limits) come from the SRS detail block — cite the path
  code next to the schema.
- Field-level errors appear on the field; form-level or server errors appear in the shared form error banner
  above the actions.
- Submit disabled while submitting and, where the SRS says so, until something changed and minimum lengths are met.
- Multi-tab forms (e.g. Dsc product): the entity is created when the first mandatory tab is saved; later tabs save
  independently; unsaved-change guard on tab/route leave.

## Modals and actions

- Destructive or moderation actions (delete, reject, suspend, cancel, unpublish) use the shared confirm modal;
  reject/suspend/cancel use the shared reason-picker modal.
- Actions available on a row come from `status × capability` (see `41-shared-patterns.mdc`), rendered by the shared
  row-actions menu.

## Feedback

- Success/failure toasts use SRS texts. Toasts never carry information that is unavailable elsewhere.
- There is no toast system yet. Adding one is a foundation task: do not build an ad hoc toast inside a feature;
  ask first.
- Heavy UI (modals with editors, charts, file import) is lazy-loaded with `next/dynamic`.

## Accessibility

- All interactive elements keyboard-reachable with visible focus; modals trap focus and restore it on close.
- Inputs have associated labels; errors are linked with `aria-describedby`; icon-only buttons have `aria-label`.
